<div class="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <%#
    min-w-0 is load-bearing: this is a flex item, and a flex item's default
    `min-width: auto` refuses to shrink below its content's minimum. The connect
    URI below is a single nowrap line ~600px wide, so without this the whole
    card is forced to that width and the page scrolls sideways on a phone.
  %>
  <div class="max-w-md w-full min-w-0 space-y-6">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">Emanator</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Sign in with your Nostr identity</p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="border rule divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-700"
      data-controller="nostr-login"
    >
      <%#
        Sign-in methods, ordered by how quickly they finish. The extension is one
        tap and appears only when one is present; the signer app is the path most
        people take; pasting a bunker link is for people who prefer to start from
        their signer. All three stay visible — nothing is behind a tab.
      %>

      <!-- 1. Browser extension (NIP-07). Revealed by JS only when window.nostr exists. -->
      <div id="nip07-section" class="hidden p-6" data-nostr-login-target="nip07Section">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          Browser extension
        </h2>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="mt-3 w-full flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg bg-amber-700 hover:bg-amber-800 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-700 text-white font-medium transition-colors disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
          data-action="click->nostr-login#loginWithExtension"
          data-nostr-login-target="extensionButton"
        >
          <svg class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.828 10.172a4 4 0 00-5.656 0l-4 4a4 4 0 105.656 5.656l1.102-1.101m-.758-4.899a4 4 0 005.656 0l4-4a4 4 0 00-5.656-5.656l-1.1 1.1"/>
          </svg>
          <span data-nostr-login-target="extensionButtonLabel">Continue with extension</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. Signer app (NIP-46, nostrconnect). -->
      <div class="p-6" data-nostr-login-target="qrSection">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          Signer app
        </h2>

        <%#
          A phone cannot scan a QR code that the same phone is displaying, so
          both affordances ship and CSS orders them by what is usable at that
          size: on a narrow screen you are almost certainly holding the device
          you would hand off to, so the button leads; at desktop width "scan it
          from my other phone" is the real flow, so the QR leads.

          Ordering only — neither is ever hidden, and no user-agent is sniffed,
          because nothing here can detect whether a signer is installed.
        %>
        <div class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-6">
          <div class="order-1 md:order-2">
            <a
              href="<%= @connect_data[:uri] %>"
              class="w-full flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 rounded-lg bg-amber-700 hover:bg-amber-800 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-700 text-white font-medium transition-colors"
            >
              <svg class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 7h6v6M19 7l-8.5 8.5M11 5H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v11a2 2 0 002 2h11a2 2 0 002-2v-5"/>
              </svg>
              Open in your signer app
            </a>
            <%#
              Not "Open in Amber": several signers register the scheme across
              platforms, the OS picks which one receives it, and naming one makes
              the button look broken on a device that has a different signer.
            %>
            <p class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
              Amber, Amethyst, or any signer on this device
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="order-2 md:order-1">
            <p class="text-center text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-3">
              Scan with a signer on another device
            </p>
            <%= render "shared/qr_phishing_warning", caption: "logs them into Emanator as you" %>
            <div class="flex justify-center">
              <%# Scale the SVG to the container so a denser QR (more relays =>
                  more modules) never overflows the card. %>
              <div class="w-full max-w-[15rem] bg-white p-3 rounded-lg ring-1 ring-gray-200 dark:ring-gray-600 [&>svg]:block [&>svg]:w-full [&>svg]:h-auto">
                <%= @qr_code.as_svg(
                  color: "000",
                  shape_rendering: "crispEdges",
                  module_size: 4,
                  standalone: true,
                  use_path: true,
                  viewbox: true
                ).html_safe %>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%# The URI itself, always reachable — it used to be the only way in on
              a phone, collapsed inside a <details> with no copy button. %>
          <div class="order-3 flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-700/60 px-3 py-2">
            <code class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate font-mono text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 select-all"><%= @connect_data[:uri] %></code>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="shrink-0 text-xs font-medium text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-800 dark:hover:text-amber-300 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-700 rounded"
              data-controller="clipboard"
              data-clipboard-text-value="<%= @connect_data[:uri] %>"
              data-action="click->clipboard#copy"
            >Copy</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. bunker:// — the signer speaks first. -->
      <div class="p-6" data-nostr-login-target="bunkerSection">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          Paste a bunker link
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          Create a connection in your signer and paste the link it gives you.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 flex gap-2">
          <%#
            Every keyboard assist is off: iOS otherwise capitalises and
            autocorrects the hex pubkey. inputmode=url puts ":" and "/" on the
            mobile keyboard without a shift.
          %>
          <label for="bunker-uri" class="sr-only">Bunker link</label>
          <input
            id="bunker-uri"
            type="text"
            placeholder="bunker://…"
            autocomplete="off"
            autocapitalize="none"
            autocorrect="off"
            spellcheck="false"
            inputmode="url"
            class="flex-1 min-w-0 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 dark:border-[color:var(--color-rule-dark)] bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 placeholder-gray-500 dark:placeholder-gray-400 focus:border-amber-500 focus:outline-none"
            data-nostr-login-target="bunkerInput"
            data-action="keydown.enter->nostr-login#connectBunker"
          />
          <button
            type="button"
            class="shrink-0 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 dark:border-[color:var(--color-rule-dark)] text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-700 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-700 transition-colors disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
            data-action="click->nostr-login#connectBunker"
            data-nostr-login-target="bunkerButton"
          >Connect</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Status: waiting / stale / expired / challenge / error -->
      <div class="p-6 space-y-3">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" data-nostr-login-target="pollingIndicator">
          <svg class="animate-spin h-4 w-4 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle class="opacity-25" cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" fill="none"/>
            <path class="opacity-75" fill="currentColor" d="M4 12a8 8 0 018-8V0C5.373 0 0 5.373 0 12h4z"/>
          </svg>
          <span data-nostr-login-target="pollingLabel">Waiting for your signer…</span>
        </div>

        <%#
          Shown after returning to this tab still unapproved. A mobile browser
          may suspend the page while the signer is in the foreground, and the
          reply to a nostrconnect handshake is ephemeral — it cannot be replayed,
          so the honest recovery is a fresh code, not a longer wait.
        %>
        <div class="hidden text-center space-y-2" data-nostr-login-target="staleNotice">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Didn't get the approval? Keep this tab open while you approve, or start over with a new code.
          </p>
          <%= link_to "Get a new code", nostr_login_path,
                data: { turbo: false },
                class: "inline-flex items-center justify-center px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 dark:border-[color:var(--color-rule-dark)] text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-700" %>
        </div>

        <%# The signer asked the user to authorize in a browser window first. %>
        <div class="hidden rounded-lg bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-900/20 p-4 text-center space-y-2" data-nostr-login-target="authChallenge">
          <p class="text-sm text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300">
            Your signer needs you to approve this in its own window.
          </p>
          <a
            href="#"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg bg-amber-700 hover:bg-amber-800 text-white text-sm font-medium"
            data-nostr-login-target="authChallengeLink"
          >Open approval page</a>
        </div>

        <div class="hidden text-center space-y-3" data-nostr-login-target="expiredNotice">
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            This code expired for your security.
          </p>
          <%= link_to "Get a new code", nostr_login_path,
                data: { turbo: false },
                class: "inline-flex items-center justify-center px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-amber-700 hover:bg-amber-800 text-white text-sm font-medium" %>
        </div>

        <div id="error-message" class="hidden rounded-lg bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-900/20 p-4" data-nostr-login-target="errorMessage" role="alert">
          <p class="text-sm text-red-700 dark:text-red-400" data-nostr-login-target="errorText"></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Data attributes for JS -->
      <div
        data-nostr-login-poll-url="<%= auth_nostr_poll_path %>"
        data-nostr-login-callback-url="<%= auth_nostr_callback_path %>"
        data-nostr-login-bunker-url="<%= auth_nostr_bunker_path %>"
        data-nostr-login-challenge="<%= session[:nip07_challenge] %>"
        data-nostr-login-domain="<%= URI(Nostr::AuthService.new.canonical_url).host %>"
        data-nostr-login-target="config"
        class="hidden"
      ></div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500">
      No account needed. Your identity is your Nostr key.
    </p>

    <details class="text-center text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer hover:text-gray-700 dark:hover:text-gray-300">
        New to Nostr? Get a signer first.
      </summary>
      <div class="border rule mt-3 space-y-2 text-left p-4">
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">On desktop:</span>
          install a NIP-07 browser extension, e.g.
          <a href="https://getalby.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 hover:underline">Alby</a>
          or
          <a href="https://github.com/fiatjaf/nos2x" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 hover:underline">nos2x</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">On mobile:</span>
          install
          <a href="https://github.com/greenart7c3/Amber" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 hover:underline">Amber</a>
          (Android), then use "Open in your signer app" above — it hands the
          connection straight to Amber on the same phone.
        </p>
        <p>
          Either one generates a Nostr key and lets you approve sign-in/posting
          requests — Emanator never sees your private key.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</div>
